 css-1uk1gs8">Making an impact: An...</h7><div style=3D"height: 40px;">Fund=
aci=C3=B3n Cuenta Conmigo is a nonprofit foundation created to support low-=
income families with a family member suffering from cancer in the Chilean p=
ublic health system. Specifically, the foundation assists families navigati=
ng the process of their child=E2=80=99s cancer treatment. This includes cov=
ering expenses and helping address needs that are not supported by the Stat=
e or other non-governmental institutions. This organization is near and dea=
r to Ana Wainer=E2=80=99s heart. Her son, Dante=E2=80=99s, close friend, Vi=
cente, was diagnosed with pre-leukemia at age 9. After long and exhausting =
treatment, he underwent a bone marrow transplant. Unfortunately, it was not=
 successful. Vicente later relapsed with Acute Myeloid Leukemia, "a diagnos=
is that profoundly changed the lives of his family and of all of us who kne=
w him and accompanied them throughout the process,=E2=80=9D Ana says. At ag=
e 11, after a long and courageous battle, Vincente passed away. =E2=80=9CDe=
spite the deep sorrow, Vicente left us invaluable life lessons and opened o=
ur eyes to a reality that often remains invisible to much of society,=E2=80=
=9D Ana says. Shortly after his passing in March 2019, Vicente=E2=80=99s pa=
rents founded Fundaci=C3=B3n Cuenta Conmigo in 2020. Ana was a co-founder o=
f the foundation and served as a volunteer member on the board of directors=
 for three years. Through her role at Lockton, she coordinated activities b=
etween Lockton and the foundation as part of their Christmas initiatives si=
nce 2022. =E2=80=9CFrom the moment I introduced the foundation at Lockton, =
the company was very open to collaborating and the response was overwhelmin=
gly positive,=E2=80=9D Ana says. =E2=80=9CWhen I invited my colleagues to p=
articipate as volunteers, everyone showed a genuine interest in helping in =
any way needed.=E2=80=9D Ana=E2=80=99s love and dedication towards this fou=
ndation have been recognized by Lockton, earning her the Lockton Cares Comm=
unity Impact Award for the Latin America region. This award celebrates Lock=
ton Associates across the globe who go above and beyond to improve their co=
mmunities through volunteering and philanthropy. Each recipient can direct =
a $25,000 donation to a charity of their choice, funded directly by the Loc=
kton family. =E2=80=9CAs first I was genuinely surprised to hear my name, f=
ollowed by a deep sense of emotion, pride, and gratitude,=E2=80=9D Ana expl=
ains. =20
The award funds were used to purchase a brand-new utility vehicle, which is=
 now used to distribute the various donations the foundation receives and d=
elivers to families undergoing treatment in public hospitals. Donations inc=
lude food, Christmas gifts, medical supplies, orthopedic equipment, and oth=
er essential items as needs arise.=20
Ana had to step down from her role on the board of directors, but this awar=
d represents the support she wished she could have continued providing. =E2=
=80=9CI feel like it is a kind of legacy that Lockton helped me leave for t=
he foundation, for Vicente, and for his family,=E2=80=9D she says.

As she becomes more familiar with Lockton culture, Ana says it was a pleasa=
nt surprise to see that the importance of culture is not something just wri=
tten on paper, but something truly reflected in the company=E2=80=99s commi=
tment to charitable causes around the world.

=E2=80=9CLockton genuinely cares,=E2=80=9D Ana says. It=E2=80=99s no secret=
 how much this foundation means to Ana, and she will continue contributing =
and encourage more people show support in any way they can. Fundaci=C3=B3n =
Cuenta Conmiga gave Ana an opportunity to discover an unfamiliar world=E2=
=80=94one that anyone could find themselves in one day. =E2=80=9CIt taught =
me to value what I have,=E2=80=9D she says. =E2=80=9CTo be more empathetic =
toward those going through difficult times." </div></div></div></div><span =
